Z||000000||GWMORGAN||12-31-1999||01:57 AM||||I tried taking out the distributor and it plain just won't come out.Is there something I'm not doing right? (I did remove  the hold down bolt).86GT.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phaeton||12-31-1999||02:04 AM||||Lotsa miles?  Assuming the housing turns free put the rotor back on and work it back and forth with a fair amount of energy while pulling up on the housing, a ridge may have developed on the distributor gear and the cam gear doesn't want to let go.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Linx||12-31-1999||03:52 AM||||nah- the o-ring has hardened.  I had the same problem; just seemed like it needed an unnatural amount of force to yank it out...and it does.  Dont be afraid- you cant break nothin'.  Just give it a good yank and it'll come up.  Be sure to replace the o-ring before you put it back in.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GWMORGAN||12-31-1999||04:05 AM||||180,000K on the motor, never been worked on, still running strong, just want to change the O-ring. It does turn freely on the shaft. I'll give it another try later today.<BR>Thanx for input.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TOM||12-31-1999||12:30 PM||||Or pry it up with a block of wood. While its out would be a good time to replace the pick up coil. They are like $12 and worth the 1/2 hour||||reg||1
